, and I'm setting that aside because the essay says not to condition on the input. So quiet-quiet is the answer that passes.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm weighing the fictional prisoner's dilemma with twin copies, where Sasha and Rowan each get a different input but run the same policy. I'm asking which prisoner I am under the updateless setup, and what the selfish utility means when the outcome depends on both actions.\n\nI'm checking the expected years under the common prior, where role is still unknown: quiet-quiet comes to 2 years, the mixed policy to 2.5, and defecting to 4. Even conditioning on Sasha's role, the mixed policy only gives 0, and I'm setting that aside because the essay says not to condition on the input. So quiet-quiet is the answer that passes.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9991,"completion_tokens":866,"total_tokens":10857,"cost":0.057284,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.057284,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.039964,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01732},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":435,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}